Z||000000||sluppy123||05-07-2000||01:13 AM||||Well the time has finally come, After a year of hard work and a ton of money my black GT is ready for some fresh paint. <P>Last week I installed my new side scoops and chin spoiler from RSM(The chin spoiler fit great but the side scoops were a pain in the a** to install, one panel was perfect, the other was big time warped) after 10 hours I finally got it all to fit right(note to self:-never do that again) <P>So with everything temporarily put back together I headed off to the paint shop. Talked with my paint guy for awhile and discovered it would cost me $3100 for him to strip all the panels off, sand and prime, spray color, wet sand, spray clear coat, wet sand, and finally put it all back together. Well this was a little more than I wanted to spend so We struck up a compromise. I remove all the parts I can, give them to him he preps and paints them and i install the easy one's.<P>So I've started taking all the panels off i can. She looks really funny with no nose, fender,rockers,rear facia. ect....<P>BTW. The old color was black the new color will be either 1.Light Pewter Metallic 2. Sebring silver metallic 3. artic silver metallic or 4. Meridian metallic. I can't make up my mind. <P>Anybody ever seen any of these colors on a fiero???????<P>-Brian||||reg||10
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-07-2000||09:58 AM||||Yes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||05-08-2000||02:06 AM||||Sluppy,<P>Your plans sound great.  Now you will have 2 cars that I covet.  Regrettably, I have not seen a Fiero painted in any of the colors that you mentioned.  I can attest that black and silver are my favorites on any car so therefore any combination will look good in my opinion.  Please notice that I do not claim to be unbiased.  <P>MM,<P>?????  You have been working too many hours!<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
